  "result": "I fixed it: `@handle`s inside fenced code blocks and inline code no longer trigger mention notifications, and the same text outside code still does.\n\nThe cause was in `src/lib/mentions.ts`. It has a `withoutCode` helper that blanks out code blocks and inline code, but `extractMentions` never used it and scanned the raw text instead. I changed that loop to scan `withoutCode(body)`. The mentions, comment-service and mention-query tests now pass; the mentions test that checks this exact case was failing before the edit.\n\nThe server (`comment-service.ts`) and the composer (`mention-textarea.tsx`) both get mentions through `resolveMentions`, so both are fixed.\n\n`highlightMentions` still styles `@handle` text inside code in rendered comments. That's only display, not notifications, so I didn't change it.",
